      <slug></slug>
      <title>Update on Gallium3D ports to AROS and Haiku</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Alt-OS</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Gallium3D is a new architecture for building 3D graphics drivers. Initially supporting Mesa and Linux graphics drivers, Gallium3D is designed to allow portability to all major operating systems and graphics interfaces.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We will be showing a quick demo of the recent progress of the Gallium3D ports to AROS and Haiku.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="61">François Revol</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>